    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The linked PR and issue make the one-line note concrete. The subject is the bundled Argo CD Notifications `on-deployed` trigger. The PR changes only notifications_catalog/install.yaml and notifications_catalog/triggers/on-deployed.yaml [ev-d7cc48e99b69], and the issue it fixes concerns this trigger's `when` condition [ev-a5387388a48d, ev-54ad0a8bb848]. The PR says that during a legitimate sync the health last transition time can come about 1 second before the operation finished time, so the trigger now allows a 1-minute gap [ev-d739527c46a6]. That is enough to write applicability (environments that use the catalog's on-deployed trigger) and consequence (the condition that decides whether an on-deployed notification is sent changes; this is informational only). The exact before/after expression is not shown, and whether deploys used to be missed is inferred from the PR wording rather than stated, so confidence is low.",
